all right when declaring bankruptcy it's  easy to think certain actions won't  affect the process eric palacios from  eric palacios and associates and  sponsors of this segment tells us three  things to avoid if you're going to  declare bankruptcy  hi i'm eric palacios and welcome to this  week's legal minute the question for  this week is what are three things you  should not do if you're going to declare  bankruptcy number one do not run up your  credit card debt or worse get cash  advances from them the bankruptcy  trustee will see this and flag your  bankruptcy as fraudulent and may dismiss  it number two do not hide assets you  might have a motorcycle a boat a utv or  other items that can be considered  luxury items if you try to hide them the  trustee will find them and your  bankruptcy will be dismissed or worse  you could face fraud charges number  three do not continue to make payments  on your debt  continuing to make payments on your  credit card debt hospital bills payday  loans is just throwing your money out  the window once you talk to your  attorney once you know you're going to  declare bankruptcy stop making all your  payments this has been the legal minute  don't forget to  download app eric palacio's legal app  we'll see you next week  if you'd like more information you can  give eric palacios and associates call  dot  702-444-7777
 

